  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="0ba4ba69-2490-5271-87c0-c8151068566c" activityNameId="a25cd4cf-5b7f-5bb0-b4bf-19ca429fae1f" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Electricity, hydropower, at pumped storage power plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Electricity, hydropower, at pumped storage power plant
This study adresses Swiss dams only. The data have been directly applied to preliminary describe dam-mixes in other alpine countries. Considering the difficulty to clearly seperate within the Swiss dams system for some of the dams function for normal electricity generation from pumping storage, the same basic information has been used for the modules describing the two functions. A representative sample of Swiss dams with a height of more than 30 metres is taken into account for calculating the numbers. Lifetime is assumed to be 150 years. The efficiency of the pumps is assumed to be 70%. The results of this module cannot be applied to describe a single unit.;
UUID: 82c2222d-1fc3-3eb9-bbea-312d16a2b69d
Includes the conversion of electricity from domestic high voltage grid to potential energy by pumping water up to the reservoir and generation of peak-load power when water flows back down to the turbine (reverse mode). The module has the same structure as the module for operation for reservoir plants.
Location: Data for Swiss avergage conditions, directly used here.
Technology: The module describes average installed technology with an efficiency of 70% (best technology has 74%).
Time period: Nicht spezifiziert
Production volume: na
Sampling: literature 
Extrapolations: see Geography/Text
Uncertainty adjustments: Data may not be representative for specific national conditions. The uncertainities calculated for the Swiss conditions have been somewhat increased, though large variation within the alpine region is not expected.
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_82c2222d-1fc3-3eb9-bbea-312d16a2b69d.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
